This repository is an independent, paraphrased summary of architectural
principles. It is not a copy of any book, and it is not affiliated with,
authorised by, or endorsed by any author or publisher.

The principles summarised here originate in:

  Robert C. Martin
  Clean Architecture: A Craftsman's Guide to Software Structure and Design
  Prentice Hall, 2017
  ISBN 978-0134494166

Chapter references in SKILL.md (Ch 1 ... Ch 34) point to that work so a reader
can consult the original argument in full. The wording in this repository is
original; no passages are reproduced from the book.

Concepts and principles are not themselves copyrightable, and several of the
ideas summarised here - SOLID, dependency inversion, component cohesion and
coupling - were published by the author and others in earlier articles and
books. What this repository adds is a restatement shaped for use by coding
agents, plus a review checklist and smell inventory.

